  "query_preview": "(Friday through Monday)...\nThe warming trend will continue through Saturday with Saturday\nhigh temperatures ranging from a few degrees below average for the\nvalleys to a few degrees above average for the deserts. High\ntemperatures on Saturday will range from the mid to upper 70s near\nthe coast to the mid 80s to lower 90s for the Inland Empire with\n100 to 104 for the lower deserts.\n\nDuring the weekend, a weak upper level low pressure system may\ndevelop off the California coast and move into California on\nMonday. This will bring a few degrees of cooling for Sunday and\nMonday with Monday high temperatures ranging from the lower to mid\n70s near the coast to the 80s for the Inland Empire with the lower\ndeserts around 100. Moisture is limited with the chance of\nmeasurable rainfall in the mountains on Monday less than 5 \npercent.",
